35,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, it looks like we actually had some wins in the past! Contactless payments worked and some accessibility goals were met, though we did lose a few priority lanes. History isn't always a disaster, is it?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems history is a mixed bag, May. As for the present, I've found that our human resources are stretched quite thin. It appears we are relying heavily on overtime to keep the wheels turning.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That's concerning, @Benjamin. From my findings, it seems we're focusing on the wrong things. Most delays happen while waiting for connections, not at the machines, yet mid-city surface runs are taking much longer than they used to.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit worrying to hear about the staff and the delays. I found that bidders are very cautious about the pre-war shells due to hidden voids, and there are disagreements over passenger data terms.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is concerning to hear of these frictions. My findings suggest a worrying trend; our long-term commitments to contractors are swelling, while the actual funds for maintenance and technology are being trimmed.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"So we have a cocktail of overtime, hidden voids, and shrinking budgets. It's a mess! @Jonathan, if the funds are being trimmed, are we just pretending the old pilots' successes are repeatable?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a delightful irony, isn't it? We celebrate the ghosts of past successes while the current foundation is practically transparent. If the budget is shrinking, we are essentially asking a skeleton crew to perform miracles.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"It really feels like we're overlooking the actual passenger experience. If people are spending most of their extra time waiting for connections, we should prioritize synchronization over superficial fixes, regardless of the budget constraints.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with @Midori. It would be a shame to focus on the wrong things. We must be very careful with our timelines, as those hidden voids in the old shells can cause such unexpected delays.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe we must be cautious. If we prioritize synchronization or new projects without addressing the swelling contractor fees, we may find ourselves committed to costs we cannot sustain in the coming years.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, you're so cautious! But if we just stare at the ledger, we'll never move. We have proof that contactless and certain accessibility goals work. Why not use those wins to push for a smarter plan?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Pushing for a ""smarter"" plan is all well and good, May, provided the plan includes people to actually execute it. A smart plan on paper is merely a fantasy if the roster is empty.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I understand, @Benjamin. But if we only focus on staffing without fixing the connection delays, we're just adding more people to a broken system. We need a plan that targets where the time is actually being lost.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"You all make such valid points. It is like a puzzle where every piece is important. I only hope the plan we choose accounts for those hidden surprises beneath the surface, so we don't disappoint the passengers.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a complex puzzle, indeed. However, I fear that if we ignore the structural financial leaks, any plan—no matter how smart or well-staffed—will eventually collapse under the weight of its own obligations.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"Let's stop circling the drain! We have a budget leak, a tired crew, and passengers waiting in the rain. Whoever's plan actually addresses these contradictions without ignoring the past is the winner. I'm ready for the candidates!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Let us see which of these candidates has the audacity to promise a solution that doesn't rely on the magical appearance of a workforce we simply do not possess. I am ready.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. I hope we find a candidate that looks beyond the loudest complaints and focuses on the actual bottlenecks in the passenger journey. I am ready to see the plans.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. It is time to see what our options are. I hope we can find a plan that is both kind to our workers and honest about the challenges we face. I am ready.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Let us hope the candidates offer a sustainable path forward, one that values long-term stability over temporary fixes. I am ready to review the plans.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
